# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# n8n flow exports — git hygiene
#
# Flow JSONs can contain hardcoded secrets (HMAC secret, Supabase service-role
# key, API keys, private ngrok URLs). N8N-A01 and N8N-V01-Worker have been
# externalized to $vars and are safe to commit. The flows listed below still
# carry inline secrets — keep them OUT of git until their secrets are moved to
# n8n Credentials/Variables.
#
# IMPORTANT: .gitignore does NOT untrack files already committed. For any flow
# below that `git ls-files` still shows as tracked, run:
#     git rm --cached "n8n/flows/<file>.json"
# (keeps your local copy) and rotate the exposed secret — it remains in history.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Local backups & helper scripts produced during refactors — never commit
*.backup-*
*.bak
_*.py

# ── Flows still holding inline secrets (DO NOT COMMIT) ───────────────────────
N8N-A03-onboarding.json
N8N-A04-brand-correction.json
N8N-A05-monthly-cycle.json
N8N-A06-extraction.json
N8N-A07-competitor-extraction.json
N8N-D02-maintenance.json
N8N-P01-instagram-publisher.json
N8N-S03-anomaly-router.json

# Belt-and-suspenders: ignore ANY *Testing Mode* export (these inline secrets
# by design) and any ad-hoc secret-bearing export not yet hardened.
*Testing Mode*.json

# Hardened & safe to commit (explicitly un-ignored):
!N8N-A01 & N8N-V01-Sub Flow.json
!N8N-V01-Worker.json
